common: default the speculative draft depth to 4

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

Measured on the phone on 2026-09-21, 4B Q8_0 on HTP0 with the 32768-row draft head and the
REPEAT splat, greedy, one free-form prompt, 128 tokens, thermal 0 and off the charger:

    depth 3  17.223 t/s   depth 5  17.275 t/s   depth 7  16.005 t/s
    depth 4  17.441 t/s   depth 6  16.951 t/s

Depth 4 is the peak, and the break-even agrees: position 4 adds 0.271 tokens per step
against a threshold of 0.232, and position 5 adds 0.240 against 0.272. Depth 4 is also
where the verify batch reaches 5 rows and crosses HTP_MM_HMX_MIN_NROWS, thus the fourth
position costs less than the third.

The value is a ceiling. A caller that measures its own acceptance takes the draft down when
the acceptance falls, which the application does with SpecPolicy.

Files:
    common/common.h

How to apply, from the llama.cpp root:

    git apply patches/spec-draft-4/0001-common-default-the-draft-depth-to-4.patch

